{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And as for Me, this is My covenant.</b> Behold, He makes a covenant with them, and what is it? \"My spirit that is upon you\" — and the kaf [in עליך] refers to Israel, which He speaks of. And the meaning of \"My spirit\" is My prophecy, as it is written: \"And it shall come to pass afterward, I will pour out My spirit\" (Joel 3:1)." "<b>And My words which I have put in your mouth.</b> And the statement is doubled, for they prophesied and the prophecy will never cease from their seed forever."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 59, :notes {0 "The kamatz in 'אכרו' appears to abbreviate אכרות ('I will cut/make'); resolved as 'He makes' reading it as אכרו with divine subject. The letter kaf in עליך is taken as referring to Israel collectively."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:23.871032338Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}